Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.710 align:start position:0%
 
well thanks for coming here today folks  i think some of you here or most of you  here last friday we announced a series  of  increased efforts on our part to reduce  if not eliminate the full demonstration  in the safest  most effective and lawful manner  possible  we talked about the surge in contain  since that time we've had 20 arrests and  charges criminal arrests and charges of  individuals who have broken the law  directly or indirectly in regards to  this demonstration  we've issued over 500 tickets to those  individuals who've come here  mostly in conveyances trucks  suvs cars  for an awful conduct  bylaws provincial offenses and criminal  code offenses we have towed vehicles and  we have towed trucks  there has been a significant decrease in  the amount of protesters and vehicles  associated to the protesters over that  time period  the large demonstration that was planned  for this weekend was significantly  smaller than the previous weekend the  previous weekend had three thousand plus  trucks not counting all the other  vehicles  ten to fifteen thousand protesters  that took a 24 7 cycle over friday  saturday and sunday  this weekend the numbers are down around  a thousand trucks  around 5000 protesters and while there  was some activity on saturday there was  almost no activity on friday or on  sunday  that is in direct reaction to our  stepped-up enforcement our surge in  contain and our aggressive intelligence  and investigation operations that have  been taking place over the last four  days and will continue until the end of  this demonstration  what particularly has occurred of a  significant nature  we went after the funding  our efforts combined with the city's  efforts eliminated the gofundme 10  million dollars are no longer accessible  to the demonstrators there are other  funding avenues that we continue to  aggressively go after through  intelligence information coordination  with financial institutions and all  three levels of government we will be  relentless in pursuing the funding that  has enabled this demonstration to  continue to this point  we're going after the fuel  we're going after any vehicle conveyance  including horseback  people carrying jerry cans  we are arresting and seizing and we are  interdicting fuel going into  the demonstrations  last night was a major public order  operation  we tried to end it through negotiation  as we always will do in every aspect  when that failed we went into a public  order operation it included covert  assets as well as investigation and  delegate intelligence assets  seven people were arrested and charged  criminally thousands of liters of  propane and fuel were seized  and we took out an oil tanker and the  entire footprint of the staging area at  coventry park that includes hot tubs and  saunas and anything else that was down  there we've erected fences in that area  and are going to secure that area so  there are no more incursions  over the course of the weekend through  negotiation efforts we peacefully and  fully resolved  the confederation park encampment no  arrests no use of force no injuries no  deaths no riots no encampment in  confederation park  it is gone we have fenced in that area  and reclaimed that territory  expectation setting let me be clear  every time we knock something down there  are attempts for it to pop up in four or  five other locations we're rapidly  deploying our resources whenever we get  a sense of another fuel depot another  staging area or anything else that  enables  the demonstration to continue we send  resources in there we reclaim that  property and we allow ourselves to get  incremental advancements towards the end  of the demonstration  over the last four days in addition to  those operations they will continue on  to be clear  we have been seeking additional  resources provincially and federally and  of course municipally  we've been working very closely with  city manager steve canalakas the mayor's  office and as and our board in order to  seek additional funds there is a formal  request that will be sent to the mayor's  office in the next hour  requesting a significant increase in  police resources civilian resources as  well as requests for significant  increases for bylaw offenses fines and  other enabling orders of government to  allow us to more fully and effectively  and quickly as well as lawfully and  safely end this demonstration  we are turning up the heat in every way  we possibly can within our operations  and enforcement as well as in our  engagement of all three levels of  government  every available ottawa police service  officer has been working for the last  four days let me repeat we have  cancelled days off  there is nobody on a day off getting  rest over the last four days some  officers are on their 14th day straight  of 12 hours in a row during the coldest  snap in in ottawa in the last 10 years  working outside continuously  no officers are on days off everyone has  been working  we are stretched to the limit but we are  100 committed to using everything we  have to end this demonstration we cannot  do it alone that is why i have been  advocating for all three levels of  government to bring whatever they can  bear and bring to bear on the permanent  sustainable lawful safe resolution of  this demonstration  the opp the rcmp at least seven  different municipal police agencies have  embedded their officers within our  incident command structure that has  allowed us to get the relief we need to  move ottawa police officers into the  aggressive mode that you have seen over  the last four days we need more we are  grateful for what they have provided but  we need more  we are advocating for more levels of  government to do more things around  provincial interprovincial and national  strategies to address what is happening  here in the nation's capital  we'll be speaking to council within the  next hour to lay out the resource  requests that we ask the mayor to send  to the provincial solicitor general and  the public safety canada to  significantly increase our resources so  we can significantly escalate our  enforcement and interdictions in and  around the demonstration sites  let me be very clear about one thing as  hard as we have worked and as much as  our people are on the breaking point  the community has worked as hard or  harder and are closer to their breaking  point the stories coming to me are  breaking my heart  i have my own officers who live in and  around those areas and they and their  children have not been able to sleep  they and their children have not been  able to go to school this is crushing  for those residents and their businesses  it has to stop and we are doing  everything we can possibly do to stop it  we need more help we're asking for that  help we're starting to receive that help  but we need more to get this done  last but not least i want to thank the  members of this police service every  single one civilian or sworn front line  or executive we have been 100 full out  on this for the last 10 days straight  and we will not rest until it's done but  we need more help i thank the frontline  men and women who've been out there in  sub 30 degree celsius temperatures for  12 hours straight i thank our  communications operators who have been  receiving hate and threats all day long  24 7. i thank our financial people for  trying to put together the resources to  sustain this i thank everybody and  anybody in our community from counselors  to bias to service providers to the  not-for-profit sector to residents to  school teachers to make this the most  livable thing that we can to get through  it we cannot do it alone we have not  been doing it alone but we are making  real strides and we will continue to  aggressively pursue that in every aspect  going forward thank you very much and  i'd love to take your questions  you know the the protesters said  the protesters laid out their plan well  in advance before coming into ottawa yes  you're turning up the heat now but all  of these plans they said they did  exactly what they said that they were  going to do and  a lot of ottawa residents say this is a  failure of the ottawa police and  ultimately the responsibility lies with  you why is this all happening the second  week into the game thank you very much  for your question um  this is an unprecedented protest  i'm not aware of anybody who has any  experience in managing large-scale  demonstrations whether they be a police  officer or whether they be a public  official who has not already gone on  record stating very clearly this is an  unprecedented protest never seen in  canada and i've heard from colleagues  around the world very rarely have they  ever seen anything like this  so i'll just finish answering my  question answering the question thank  you  so yes there were certainly indications  around which this would be a  demonstration all of our negotiations  with the corps convoy stated that they  would be here on friday and they would  leave on sunday  those negotiations were well in place  days in advance before they came  while there were fringe elements that  said everything from insurrection  through to negotiation  our core negotiations were a  demonstration for three days in the  nation's capital and the return of of  those vehicles and demonstrators to the  parts of canada they came from that is  what we planned for that is what we  executed there was a success around  containing that as it turned into more  than a demonstration we have pivoted and  we pivoted immediately we needed more  resources to deal with a occupation than  with a demonstration i have worked  continuously 18 hour days to get those  resources our partners have started to  bring those resources to beer and as  they come in and as we reduce the size  of the footprint that has been in place  for the last 10 days we redeploy those  resources now we can go on the offensive  that's what we've been doing to great  effect  for clarification though chief are you  saying  that the ottawa police were caught off  guard that the protesters stayed as long  as they stayed  so the ottawa police service have been  able to quell the la the large  demonstration that came in as it's  turned into an occupation we've been  able to pivot and get the resources to  go on offense to remove that demonstrate  occupation while still managing the  elements of the demonstration  we have seen the challenges to our  neighborhoods and our businesses we've  seen the challenges to our officers in  delivering on that we are making  significant progress since we've made  that pivot over the last four days we  need more resources to drive those  successes even further and we might need  more levels of government to play their  role in the overall sustainable end to  this demonstration why did it take a ten  days for the ottawa police to start  confiscating fuel from the protesters  i'm not sure that's an accurate  statement we have been here  at no point thank you very much for your  question we have been introducing the  fuel to the extent that we can we did  not have the resources early in the week  as we get more resources we're able to  do more interdictions that's why we  could do the operation last night to the  scale that we did we need to maintain  and increase these resources so that we  cannot just get on the fuel we can get  to the trucks themselves  please see if there's still uh  demonstrators filling their trucks with  fuel we spoke to protesters at the  coventry site this morning after last  night's raid uh how they still have two  days worth of heating fuel and their  continent will be able to replenish that  what do you believe last night's  operation  accomplished in terms of bringing this  demonstration to the net thank you  excellent question again we've been  trying to say this this is not a simple  demonstration where if you deal with one  set of charges or one particular  location that's the end there is a level  of sustainability financial capability  determined commitment around whatever  the range of causes and i've lost track  of all the range of causes where we get  a success in one area we get an  immediate counter reaction in multiple  other areas it's not like a consecutive  movement end that then deal with that  and then deal with that that has been  the challenge from the beginning that is  why the current structure of this police  service the funding and resources of  this police service is not sufficient to  deal with all of this we need more  resources more help with what we've got  we've made significant impact but we're  going to need a lot more to really get  on top of this situation  that letter is being drafted to the  mayor i'm sure it'll become a very  public document very soon i'm sending of  the mayor he will be sending it to the  solicitor general and then on to public  safety canada we've had meetings as of  this morning with those two levels of  government they know what is coming  their way  they will have it within the next hour  those discussions will continue on no  doubt this evening  we've been making requests since before  they arrived in town we've been  receiving resources as everyone gets an  understanding of the level that we've  needed but we're not going incremental  anymore we're asking for a major push of  resources to come into the next 72 hours  thank you very much folks thank you  questions from four reporters really  that's it  [Music]

